TEXT 1456 296 Left 2 ;From ADC datasheet:\nInput Capacitance: 7 pF\nInput capacitance refers to the effective capacitance \nbetween one differential input pin and AVSS.\n \nThere is no info about input resistance. We will not model it.
TEXT 744 1488 Left 2 !.include "../../../../../../03_SubsystemDesign/ElectronicHardware/Model/AFE.sub"
TEXT -16 488 Left 2 ;Pulse model assumptions for AFE validation\n \nSensor: MICROFC-60035-SMT (2 devices in parallel)\nMicrocell recharge time constant tau_cell = 95 ns (datasheet)\nNaI(Tl) scintillation decay time approx 230 ns (dominant pulse tail)\n \nEffective current pulse decay constant tau_eff approx 200-250 ns\n \nPulse width PW >= 5*tau_eff to ensure full charge delivery\nExample: tau_eff = 230 ns -> 5*tau = 1.15 us\n \nPeriod T >= PW + 3*tau_eff to prevent pulse overlap\nRecommended T >= 3 us for clean pulse separation\n \nNote:\nCSA feedback time constant tau_feedback = Rf * Cf = 100M * 270p = 27 ms\nBaseline recovery is therefore much slower than pulse width.\nSimulation period is chosen for pulse separation, not full baseline reset.\n \nRise/Fall time TR/TF = 1 ns\n(negligible compared to system bandwidth 3-6 MHz)\n \nIamp is swept to produce Vout up to >= 2.0 Vpp\n \nUsed to verify:\n  - Sensor maximum amplitude\n  - Front-end gain scaling\n  - ADC full-scale utilization\n  - Saturation margin\n \nGoals:\n  - Avoid clipping at maximum expected energy\n  - Avoid under-utilizing ADC dynamic range
TEXT 2112 1208 Left 2 !.param tau_scint=230n\n.param t0=100n\n \n.step param Iamp list 0.2m 0.5m 1m 2m 4m 6m 8m 10m 15m\n \n \n \n.tran 0 6u 0 1n
